From c0f3084dd92faf7db4136527c03acf2b1aa5db9e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 19:09:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix render pipeline, API error handling, UI wiring and Docker
 setup

Rendering
- sandbox: install Playwright's ffmpeg (record_video needs it; every render
  failed without it) and replace the libespeak1 package with libespeak-ng1
- render.py: mix narration into the MP4 (it was generated but never used),
  trim the recording to the storyboard length aligned to page start, define
  __VIDEO_* flags before page scripts run, allow file:// module scripts, and
  report browser console/network errors in the result
- tts.py: read text from a file (no argv length / leading-dash problems),
  drop stale output before synthesizing, clamp volume

Backend
- validation: no longer crashes on malformed storyboards; a large final.mp4
  no longer fails every later validation; render now requires index.html and
  storyboard.json up front; reject bool durations and missing narration files
- tools: even-dimension/fps checks, path hardening for write_source, extension
  checks for text assets, no duplicate narration entries, stale-audio guard
- docker_runner: kill the container on timeout (it kept running), writable
  HOME on the read-only sandbox, HOST_PROJECT_ROOT for compose, truncated
  errors and a hint when the daemon/image is missing
- main/project: validate project ids, 404 instead of creating stray dirs,
  upload size limit (413), real status codes, optional request bodies,
  no-store video responses
- agent: accept empty tool arguments, string storyboards, name unknown tools;
  the model can only ingest host paths the user wrote themselves

Frontend
- validate button read r.ok but the API returns `valid`
- render handler pointed at a /render-file route that does not exist; use
  /video, and hide a stale video when switching projects

Infra / docs
- real API Dockerfile (it only contained comments), compose publishes on
  loopback and maps the host project path, .dockerignore
- README: remove corrupted UTF-16 tail, fix render output path, document
  narration, compose and tests
- add tests (62) and requirements-dev.txt

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
